course: dictionary
lesson: 7607
title: Priority: what comes first
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A priority is something that matters more than other things, so it must be done or dealt with first. Look at the words around it. «Safety is our top priority» tells you that safety comes before everything else.
explain: Priority can also mean the right to go first or be served first. «Many buses and trains have priority seats near the doors just for them.» The clue is just for them: these seats are kept for certain people, so those people get to sit there first. Ask yourself: who goes first here?
explain: Use the swap check. Put "the most important thing" in place of priority: "Safety is our top most important thing" still makes sense, so you have found the meaning. Phrases like give priority to and get your priorities right show that you are choosing what to do first.
fact: A priority is something that is more important than other things and must be done first.
fact: A priority can also be the right to go first or be served first.
fact: «Top priority» means the most important thing of all.
fact: «A budget is a plan for how to spend a fixed amount of money, so a council must choose a priority, like a playground or a library.» Here the priority is the thing that gets the money first.
fact: Priority is a noun, and its plural is priorities.
exercise: «Safety is our top priority.» What does priority mean here? | *Something that is more important and must come first | A kind of bus ticket | A small, quiet place to sit | Something that is always forgotten
exercise: «Many buses and trains have priority seats for people who find standing hard.» Who are the priority seats for? | Drivers only | Anyone who wants to sit down | *People who find standing hard | People who are in a hurry
exercise: Which phrase means the most important thing of all? | give priority to | get your priorities right | priority seats | *top priority
test: A council has money for one project and must give priority to a playground or a library. What does give priority to mean? | *Choose to deal with it first | Ask a friend to pick | Forget about it completely | Build it at the end of the year
test: «In traffic, some vehicles have priority.» What does this mean? | *Some vehicles may go first | All vehicles must stop | Vehicles should drive backwards | Only buses are allowed on the road
exam: Ella says priority is just another word for a seat. Which sentence shows what priority really means? | Priorities are only for adults | A priority is always a seat | *Homework before games is a priority, so it gets done first | Priority means a kind of fast car
